From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: qcom: rpmhpd: Keep MX at or above MMCX on SC8280XP

The memories of the multimedia blocks run from MX, so MX must not sit
below MMCX. The Windows PEP for this SoC (qcpep8280.sys) makes its MMCX
node depend on MX and raises MX to the same level before MMCX; Linux
leaves MX to whatever the other subsystems vote, which can be low with
the display off while the camera runs MMCX at TURBO.

Give SC8280XP's MMCX (and its active-only peer) MX as parent, as
cx_w_mx_parent does for CX elsewhere. SA8540P shares the table indexes
but is left alone here, untested.

Tested: boots, display on with MX following MMCX at 416; with the
display off, the camera full size path streams with MMCX and MX both at
384, both back to 0 when idle.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
index 63120e703..355842c95 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
@@ -167,6 +167,22 @@ static struct rpmhpd mmcx_ao_w_cx_parent = {
 	.res_name = "mmcx.lvl",
 };
 
+static struct rpmhpd mmcx_ao_w_mx_parent;
+static struct rpmhpd mmcx_w_mx_parent = {
+	.pd = { .name = "mmcx", },
+	.peer = &mmcx_ao_w_mx_parent,
+	.parent = &mx.pd,
+	.res_name = "mmcx.lvl",
+};
+
+static struct rpmhpd mmcx_ao_w_mx_parent = {
+	.pd = { .name = "mmcx_ao", },
+	.active_only = true,
+	.peer = &mmcx_w_mx_parent,
+	.parent = &mx_ao.pd,
+	.res_name = "mmcx.lvl",
+};
+
 static struct rpmhpd mss = {
 	.pd = { .name = "mss", },
 	.res_name = "mss.lvl",
@@ -788,8 +804,8 @@ static struct rpmhpd *sc8280xp_rpmhpds[] = {
 	[SC8280XP_GFX] = &gfx,
 	[SC8280XP_LCX] = &lcx,
 	[SC8280XP_LMX] = &lmx,
-	[SC8280XP_MMCX] = &mmcx,
-	[SC8280XP_MMCX_AO] = &mmcx_ao,
+	[SC8280XP_MMCX] = &mmcx_w_mx_parent,
+	[SC8280XP_MMCX_AO] = &mmcx_ao_w_mx_parent,
 	[SC8280XP_MX] = &mx,
 	[SC8280XP_MX_AO] = &mx_ao,
 	[SC8280XP_MXC] = &mxc,
